      "content": "In urban modeling, \"friction\" refers to non-system throughput capacity delays caused by external influences, such as ramp metering delays, pedestrian and cyclist congestion, and emergency vehicle breaching precedence lanes. It's more nuanced than just braking/accessing acceleration cycles, typically quantified by using Green Town/Stop/Wait percentages where high counts of bus/stops wins.",
